{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"41e51e2ba7fd1f89ef55aa1d30bdebcb50bf5d5995874f7a7717cd7a6911427e","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler snapshot schema enforcement","key_entities":["_engine/rebar_reconciler/_snapshot_schema.py","src/rebar/schemas/","fetcher.py","schemas.load()","jsonschema","Draft202012Validator","python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types","_build-and-test.yml","bridge_state/snapshots/","tests/fixtures/jira/","docs/adr/0004"],"problem_keywords":["schema enforcement","snapshot-entry contract","schema drift","data validation","contract testing"],"propositions":["The snapshot-entry schema contract is defined in a hand-rolled Python module outside the centralized schema machinery, making it unenforced while 90 sibling schemas are automatically validated.","The fetcher producer never imports the snapshot schema despite being intended to validate against it, leaving a data-destroying CLEAR path unguarded.","A redacted fixture covering populated, parent-absent, and empty snapshot shapes must be created in tests/fixtures/jira/ to support testing the contract enforcement.","The snapshot-entry contract must be migrated into src/rebar/schemas/ and integrated with the existing jsonschema validation and generated-types drift gate at CI."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787403451801857001,"uuid":"56cdcca9-e35a-4973-b264-51e4ac432d67"}